            <title><![CDATA[Google just redesigned the search box for the first time in 25 years — here’s why it matters more than you think.]]></title>
            <link>https://venturebeat.com/technology/google-just-redesigned-the-search-box-for-the-first-time-in-25-years-heres-why-it-matters-more-than-you-think</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">5M2gv6mk7MEHXAvBa4H7z0</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 19 May 2026 17:45:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>For a quarter century, the Google search box has been one of the most recognizable interfaces in computing: a thin white rectangle, a blinking cursor, a few typed words, and a list of blue links. On Tuesday, Google will formally retire that paradigm.</p><p><a href="https://venturebeat.com/technology/google-just-redesigned-the-search-box-for-the-first-time-in-25-years-heres-why-it-matters-more-than-you-think">Read more</a></p>]]></description>
            <author>michael.nunez@venturebeat.com (Michael Nuñez)</author>
            <category>Technology</category>
            <category>Infrastructure</category>
            <category>Business</category>
            <category>AI</category>
